This package ships no third-party runtime dependencies. It uses only the
Node.js standard library (>=22) and, on Linux/macOS, an optional native thin
client compiled from the Go source in `native/`.

The benchmark harness in `bench/` is development-only and depends on the
following packages, each under its own license:

  - agent-browser (Apache-2.0)
  - @playwright/cli, @playwright/mcp (Apache-2.0)
  - chrome-devtools-mcp (Apache-2.0)
  - dev-browser
  - @modelcontextprotocol/sdk (MIT)
  - js-tiktoken (MIT)

Monad-browser is not affiliated with Google, Microsoft, Vercel or any other
project named above; those names are used only to describe interoperability.
